@startuml
' `!pragma useVerticalIf on`: the tests of an `if` with `elseif`s one below
' the other, each branch right of its test, the `else` below the last; the
' branches come together on a rail on the right, as PlantUML draws them.
!pragma useVerticalIf on
start
if (Paid?) then (yes)
  :Ship it;
(no) elseif (Promised?) then (yes)
elseif (Asked twice?) then (yes)
  -> remind;
  :Send a reminder;
  :Wait a week;
elseif (Lost?) then (yes)
  :Write it off;
  stop
else (nothing)
  :Ask again;
endif
:Done;
stop
@enduml
